Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Your Honor

asr-006797
04:41:59.590 --> 04:42:11.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mr. President, according to DBM, yung unreleased sin tax, their figure is 143 billion.

asr-006797-split-2
04:42:11.140 --> 04:42:13.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sorry, what is 143?

asr-006797-split-3
04:42:13.600 --> 04:42:18.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sin tax. Wala pa yung PCSO and PAGCOR.

asr-006797-split-4
04:42:18.500 --> 04:42:22.850
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: From what year to what year?

asr-006797-split-5
04:42:22.850 --> 04:42:25.990
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 2022 up to 2027.

asr-006797-split-6
04:42:25.990 --> 04:42:29.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: '23 tayo eh. What is it? 100?

asr-006798
04:42:29.500 --> 04:42:31.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 43. 143.

asr-006798-split-2
04:42:31.220 --> 04:42:58.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Most likely because I asked my staff to cut it to 2023 to be fair to this administration. Hindi naman walang kinalaman before that, but they will argue they were not around then. So I cut it at 2023 and the total is 133. We just have to check the 2022 figures and it is probably 10 billion. Most likely we have the same figures.

asr-006799
04:42:58.040 --> 04:43:09.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So where's that?

asr-006799-split-2
04:43:09.800 --> 04:43:20.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mr. President, the DBM committed they will slowly return it, depending on fiscal space. Dahan-dahan daw nila ibabalik.

asr-006799-split-3
04:43:20.700 --> 04:43:28.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, and I have no choice but to trust that this is understood to be legally due.

asr-006800
04:43:28.040 --> 04:43:58.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It must be paid back. I would like to see a plan. Because if I see a plan that includes some part funding in God knows what project, then I will raise hell, because this goes directly to a mother who is dying of breast cancer, a father who is dying of testicular cancer, prostate cancer.

asr-006811
04:43:59.820 --> 04:44:00.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Your Honor,

asr-006812
04:44:00.820 --> 04:44:02.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: they committed that they will provide

asr-006813
04:44:02.680 --> 04:44:03.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the...

asr-006814
04:44:03.860 --> 04:44:04.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Let's have a plan.

asr-006815
04:44:05.000 --> 04:44:05.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Let's have a plan.

asr-006816
04:44:05.880 --> 04:44:07.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi, medyo mahirap yung walang plan eh.

asr-006817
04:44:07.640 --> 04:44:08.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Madaling sabihin na

asr-006818
04:44:08.760 --> 04:44:09.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: wala eh.

asr-006819
04:44:09.960 --> 04:44:10.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Hindi, wag yung wala.

asr-006820
04:44:10.960 --> 04:44:11.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: May plan dapat.

asr-006821
04:44:12.560 --> 04:44:13.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Oh, good job.

asr-006822
04:44:15.860 --> 04:44:16.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So,

asr-006823
04:44:16.340 --> 04:44:17.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I have a question.

asr-006824
04:44:18.640 --> 04:44:20.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nag-alabas nila doon sa DSM,

asr-006825
04:44:20.860 --> 04:44:22.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: yung total

asr-006826
04:44:22.000 --> 04:44:23.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: na nakukuha from Santra.

asr-006827
04:44:24.040 --> 04:44:24.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So,

asr-006828
04:44:24.500 --> 04:44:25.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: kung may total ka nang lalabas,

asr-006829
04:44:25.840 --> 04:44:30.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Bakit mo masasabi na nakaka-prompt yung game sa competition?

asr-006830
04:44:30.140 --> 04:44:44.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ...

asr-006831
04:44:49.460 --> 04:44:50.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: ...

asr-006832
04:44:50.420 --> 04:44:58.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: ...

asr-006833
04:45:00.000 --> 04:45:07.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sige, I have something more on syntax, Mr. President, but I'll move on to another point because I asked my staff to just write it down.

asr-006834
04:45:09.120 --> 04:45:14.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think we have similar numbers. I also have for the PAGCOR and PCSO collection.

asr-006835
04:45:16.320 --> 04:45:19.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I already gave you the totals, but I'll be happy to share the details.

asr-006836
04:45:19.760 --> 04:45:33.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, before I leave PhilHealth, PhilHealth has stated that it needs an additional 170 billion to cover the subsidy for indirect contributors.

asr-006837
04:45:34.440 --> 04:45:40.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, who are indirect contributors? Ito yung senior citizens, PWDs, solo parents, national athletes, and 4Ps.

asr-006838
04:45:40.900 --> 04:45:49.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, these are the sectors that are deemed unable or hirap to provide their own.

asr-006839
04:45:49.620 --> 04:45:49.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Alam natin, ito yung senior citizens, PWDs, solo parents, national athletes, and 4Ps.

asr-006840
04:45:49.740 --> 04:45:51.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, naalam mo din yan, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006841
04:45:52.220 --> 04:45:58.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, the government subsidizes these indirect contributors.

asr-006842
04:45:59.360 --> 04:46:09.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And so, if you ask, because that's what I thought was the tenor of the response I got during the August hearing na magkakonsulta sa PhilHealth sa need.

asr-006843
04:46:09.420 --> 04:46:14.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, first of all, iba yung need. Iba yung kung ano yung sinabi ni Batas, ibigay niyo.

asr-006844
04:46:14.140 --> 04:46:19.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, here I am also saying, well, okay, speaking of need, this is the declared need.

asr-006845
04:46:19.180 --> 04:46:23.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: 170 billion to cover the indirect contributors.

asr-006846
04:46:23.480 --> 04:46:28.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I remember last year and the previous years when I chaired the budget of the Committee on Health,

asr-006847
04:46:28.780 --> 04:46:34.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: natanong ako na paano kung kulang yung pondo for the indirect contributors.

asr-006848
04:46:34.560 --> 04:46:39.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And the response of PhilHealth is, wala namang problema, we will never turn anyone away.

asr-006849
04:46:40.320 --> 04:46:45.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Wala nga, pero nagkakanda utang-utang na lahat ng tao.

asr-006850
04:46:45.360 --> 04:46:49.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, yung hospital, inaantay na bayaran siya ng PhilHealth.

asr-006851
04:46:49.180 --> 04:46:53.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung tao, nakapila sa kung saan-saang ayuda para, alam mo yan, Mr. Chairman,

asr-006852
04:46:53.620 --> 04:46:56.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: humingi ng additional funding para dun sa gastos niya.

asr-006853
04:46:56.340 --> 04:47:00.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi nga, the funding in the system is not enough.

asr-006854
04:47:00.880 --> 04:47:09.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It is identified as 170B, supposedly, by actuarial studies that hopefully we can rely on.

asr-006855
04:47:10.300 --> 04:47:12.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero wala naman tayong binibigay na ganung subsidy.

asr-006856
04:47:12.380 --> 04:47:17.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, kulang ang pondo. And that is why, kulang.

asr-006857
04:47:17.420 --> 04:47:18.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: May nakapila dyan.

asr-006858
04:47:19.020 --> 04:47:19.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: May...

asr-006859
04:47:19.180 --> 04:47:23.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: May nakapila dyan, whether sa mayor, sa governor, sa atin.

asr-006860
04:47:23.440 --> 04:47:24.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yun po yung reason.

asr-006861
04:47:24.300 --> 04:47:26.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, anyway, do you agree with me, Mr. Chairman?

asr-006862
04:47:26.080 --> 04:47:26.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: You're nodding your head.

asr-006863
04:47:27.000 --> 04:47:29.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, let the record show that the chairman is nodding his head.

asr-006864
04:47:32.320 --> 04:47:39.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Well, actually, that's what we intended to remove or to address when we passed the UHC.

asr-006865
04:47:39.340 --> 04:47:48.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: For patients or people to go to officials.

asr-006866
04:47:48.240 --> 04:47:50.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: To line up the PAC or PCSO.

asr-006867
04:47:50.820 --> 04:47:56.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Just to be able to pay their further medical expenses.

asr-006868
04:47:56.680 --> 04:48:01.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But I'm hoping that, hopefully, we are entering the eighth year of the UHC implementation.

asr-006869
04:48:02.340 --> 04:48:05.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hopefully, that everything will really be improved in the next two years.

asr-006870
04:48:06.220 --> 04:48:10.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As we achieve, since it's a 10-year program, we are hoping that by the 10th year,

asr-006871
04:48:10.940 --> 04:48:15.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: it will really be close to full implementation, Your Honor, Mr. President.

asr-006872
04:48:15.240 --> 04:48:18.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: As the chairman also knows,

asr-006873
04:48:18.240 --> 04:48:23.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: one way that we can make the billing, the whole, not just the billing system,

asr-006874
04:48:23.520 --> 04:48:29.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: but the bill itself more reflective of the true cost is the need to shift to the DRG.

asr-006875
04:48:29.900 --> 04:48:31.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's a bit technical, so di na ako mapapakahaba.

asr-006876
04:48:32.200 --> 04:48:36.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero para mag-shift tayo sa DRG, may gasos din yun.

asr-006877
04:48:36.920 --> 04:48:45.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And supposedly, itong mga subsidies natin, government subsidies, would be able to fund this DRG.

asr-006878
04:48:45.380 --> 04:48:47.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, a lot of our case rates are so...

asr-006879
04:48:47.860 --> 04:48:48.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, a lot of our case rates are so...

asr-006880
04:48:48.220 --> 04:48:50.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, a lot of our case rates are so updated, and they're very simple.

asr-006881
04:48:50.260 --> 04:48:54.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: There are so many kinds of pneumonia, and for the longest time, isa lang yung bill natin sa simonya.

asr-006882
04:48:54.940 --> 04:48:59.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I don't know, Secretary, if you're familiar with that situation, but that is where we are.

asr-006883
04:48:59.660 --> 04:49:10.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And for it to be technically and accurately, you know, dissected into all these different kinds of classifications of pneumonia,

asr-006884
04:49:11.240 --> 04:49:13.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: it has to really be done properly.

asr-006885
04:49:13.180 --> 04:49:14.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: You know that, Mr. Chairman?

asr-006886
04:49:14.160 --> 04:49:18.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I'm just saying, without this funding, it's just a vicious cycle.

asr-006887
04:49:18.220 --> 04:49:26.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And the need for all sorts of ayuda will remain because we are not funding properly,

asr-006888
04:49:26.620 --> 04:49:29.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: which by law, we worked on to address.

asr-006889
04:49:30.220 --> 04:49:31.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But then we're not funding it.

asr-006890
04:49:31.620 --> 04:49:32.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, it doesn't happen.

asr-006891
04:49:32.740 --> 04:49:32.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-006892
04:49:34.480 --> 04:49:46.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And also, put on record that according to PIDs, the country's out-of-pocket spending is at roughly 43%.

asr-006893
04:49:46.400 --> 04:49:48.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And this is way above...

asr-006894
04:49:48.440 --> 04:49:52.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: what is the WHO standard of 20 to 25%.

asr-006895
04:49:52.160 --> 04:49:53.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, malayo pa tayo.

asr-006896
04:49:53.540 --> 04:49:55.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero, if you look at the...

asr-006897
04:49:55.320 --> 04:49:56.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What is that term?

asr-006898
04:49:56.500 --> 04:49:57.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung catastrophic?

asr-006899
04:49:57.860 --> 04:49:59.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung mga catastrophic illnesses?

asr-006900
04:50:01.120 --> 04:50:06.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Then, I think the out-of-pocket contribution is probably 90% or 95%.

asr-006901
04:50:06.420 --> 04:50:10.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because we have a fund for catastrophic, but again, it's not enough.

asr-006902
04:50:10.660 --> 04:50:13.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, anyway, that's where we are.

asr-006903
04:50:13.420 --> 04:50:16.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, I will move on, Mr. Chairman, Mr. President.

asr-006904
04:50:18.220 --> 04:50:34.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I move on, Mr. President, to our El Nino response.

asr-006905
04:50:34.500 --> 04:50:40.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The reason I bring it up here is because after today,

asr-006906
04:50:40.480 --> 04:50:44.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: we will be dealing with the individual budgets of different agencies.

asr-006907
04:50:44.140 --> 04:50:48.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And we will receive individualized responses.

asr-006908
04:50:48.520 --> 04:50:54.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I want to ask questions with a whole-of-government approach.

asr-006909
04:50:56.240 --> 04:51:01.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, DOST and PAGASA already warned us of this El Nino that will hit us...

asr-006910
04:51:01.480 --> 04:51:04.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that has already hit us between September and December 2026,

asr-006911
04:51:05.120 --> 04:51:08.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and then will persist through the first half of 2027.

asr-006912
04:51:08.900 --> 04:51:16.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: In 2023, PBBM ordered the creation of a coordinating council led by NDRRMC.

asr-006913
04:51:16.500 --> 04:51:17.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: 2023.

asr-006914
04:51:18.220 --> 04:51:24.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Based on the National Action Plan for El Nino, at that time, the government identified sectors

asr-006915
04:51:24.800 --> 04:51:28.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: where plans and activities are being laid out to mitigate the effects of El Nino.

asr-006916
04:51:28.440 --> 04:51:31.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Water, food, power, health, and public safety.

asr-006917
04:51:32.620 --> 04:51:33.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That was 2023.

asr-006918
04:51:34.540 --> 04:51:35.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Today, it is 2026.

asr-006919
04:51:35.900 --> 04:51:40.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The government announced that PBBM will lead the task force meetings

asr-006920
04:51:40.740 --> 04:51:44.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and directly issue orders on the course of action to be taken.

asr-006921
04:51:48.220 --> 04:51:52.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, may we know more details about this?

asr-006922
04:51:53.280 --> 04:51:55.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Is there an action plan?

asr-006923
04:51:55.920 --> 04:51:58.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because from the hearings we had,

asr-006924
04:51:59.820 --> 04:52:02.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: medyo kanya-kanyang action plan.

asr-006949
04:52:18.220 --> 04:52:25.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: For the record, the Office of Civil Defense,

asr-006950
04:52:26.020 --> 04:52:28.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think a month ago or two,

asr-006951
04:52:28.360 --> 04:52:32.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: reported that the government is set to implement its El Nino action plan.

asr-006952
04:52:32.620 --> 04:52:38.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Maybe we can see this so that when we call the other agencies involved,

asr-006953
04:52:39.040 --> 04:52:42.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: because DOH is involved, DA is involved, DSWD is involved,

asr-006954
04:52:42.620 --> 04:52:46.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: we can also try to help ensure that they are coordinated.

asr-006955
04:52:48.220 --> 04:52:57.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Are you correct that it's OCD that's heading the task force,

asr-006956
04:52:57.460 --> 04:52:59.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: according to the economic managers?

asr-006957
04:53:01.100 --> 04:53:08.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But we have included in the budget, in the Senate,

asr-006958
04:53:08.180 --> 04:53:18.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we have included in some programs like the assistance to farmers and fisher folks,

asr-006959
04:53:18.220 --> 04:53:23.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: under the DA, direct assistance, about 5 billion.

asr-006960
04:53:23.940 --> 04:53:25.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We allotted 5 billion.

asr-006961
04:53:28.140 --> 04:53:34.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: There, the buffer for NFA, there's a buffer stocking program of 11.2 billion.

asr-006962
04:53:38.620 --> 04:53:45.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And then also construction, rehabilitation of water supply, about 7.3 billion.

asr-006963
04:53:45.960 --> 04:53:47.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So for DPWH.

asr-006964
04:53:48.220 --> 04:53:50.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And rainwater collector systems.

asr-006965
04:53:52.240 --> 04:53:58.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And then the NDRM, the National Disaster Risk Reduction Management,

asr-006966
04:53:58.580 --> 04:54:04.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: there's a 45.7 billion calamity fund.

asr-006967
04:54:05.060 --> 04:54:09.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But we reduced it by, the House reduced it to 35

asr-006968
04:54:09.200 --> 04:54:14.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: because nilagay nila sa DA, direct assistance to farmers and fisher folks.

asr-006969
04:54:14.540 --> 04:54:15.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-006970
04:54:18.220 --> 04:54:20.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's okay, Mr. President, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006971
04:54:21.740 --> 04:54:27.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I understand that you're highlighting the different funding in different agencies.

asr-006972
04:54:27.500 --> 04:54:29.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero I think what's very important is who's in charge?

asr-006973
04:54:30.260 --> 04:54:32.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So when there's a problem, like somebody should be coordinating.

asr-006974
04:54:32.780 --> 04:54:37.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because even in the small agencies that I have been assigned to oversee,

asr-006975
04:54:37.580 --> 04:54:39.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I can already see some duplications.

asr-006976
04:54:40.660 --> 04:54:41.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So who's in charge of that?

asr-006977
04:54:42.120 --> 04:54:44.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Who do we talk to when these things are happening?

asr-006978
04:54:45.500 --> 04:54:47.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And when we hear of lack of coordination?

asr-006979
04:54:48.220 --> 04:55:00.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It's the OCD, Yusec Harold Cabreros, under DND.

asr-006980
04:55:02.000 --> 04:55:03.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So hindi na po si Presidente.

asr-006981
04:55:03.920 --> 04:55:05.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi that was announced in October 1.

asr-006982
04:55:06.780 --> 04:55:08.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Si Presidente daw ang in charge.

asr-006983
04:55:13.180 --> 04:55:16.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Para clear lang tayo kung sino talaga in charge.

asr-006984
04:55:18.220 --> 04:55:21.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The OCD will function as the Secretariat.

asr-006985
04:55:21.860 --> 04:55:23.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Of course, it's the President who will head.

asr-006986
04:55:24.540 --> 04:55:27.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And just for that record, Your Honor, Mr. President,

asr-006987
04:55:27.660 --> 04:55:38.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: for NEP level, a total of 104 billion is allotted for El Nino preparation.

asr-006988
04:55:39.340 --> 04:55:41.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sorry again, can you repeat it?

asr-006989
04:55:41.580 --> 04:55:44.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 104 billion.

asr-006990
04:55:45.200 --> 04:55:45.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: What is it?

asr-006991
04:55:45.780 --> 04:55:48.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In distributed different agencies.

asr-006992
04:55:48.220 --> 04:55:58.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So from DPWH, to DOLE, to DSWD, DND, and DA, and even DNR.

asr-006993
04:55:59.080 --> 04:56:03.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So we'll just give you a copy, Your Honor, Mr. President,

asr-006994
04:56:04.360 --> 04:56:09.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: for the El Nino preparedness response, the proposed programs and activities and projects.

asr-006995
04:56:10.540 --> 04:56:12.920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, thank you so much for that, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006996
04:56:18.220 --> 04:56:23.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'll repeat something I always repeat in every budget season.

asr-006997
04:56:24.300 --> 04:56:28.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The Senate has a committee on sustainable development goals, innovations, and futures thinking.

asr-006998
04:56:28.480 --> 04:56:36.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I think I mentioned this during the hearing, that when I chaired the budget of various committees,

asr-006999
04:56:37.080 --> 04:56:43.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'd like to think I was able to convince them on the importance of having a futures thinking office.

asr-007000
04:56:44.140 --> 04:56:48.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So if, unfortunately, I think DA doesn't have it.

asr-007001
04:56:48.220 --> 04:56:52.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm not aware that DA has.

asr-007002
04:56:52.880 --> 04:56:59.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And so when we are confronted with calamities like this, it's not that difficult to predict.

asr-007003
04:56:59.940 --> 04:57:00.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It really isn't.

asr-007004
04:57:02.160 --> 04:57:07.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That really is the purpose of having a futures thinking office that doesn't do anything but solely predict the future.

asr-007005
04:57:08.160 --> 04:57:09.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Why do we have to do that?

asr-007006
04:57:09.400 --> 04:57:17.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Well, it is our job to create programs and to fund programs that will ensure intergenerational fairness.

asr-007007
04:57:18.520 --> 04:57:20.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So again, I said this before, this is not new.

asr-007008
04:57:20.920 --> 04:57:23.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Some countries prepare seven generations ahead.

asr-007009
04:57:23.820 --> 04:57:28.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But when you're confronted with a calamity, it's hard to think of those seven generations ahead

asr-007010
04:57:28.480 --> 04:57:34.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: because you're thinking of the survival of every family that's living right now today in 2026.

asr-007011
04:57:34.500 --> 04:57:43.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And that's why we need such an office, I think maybe under NEDA or, I don't know, a coordinating body

asr-007012
04:57:43.740 --> 04:57:47.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: so that we can be sure that we are not sacrificing the future.

asr-007013
04:57:48.220 --> 04:57:55.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: For the present need and vice versa, we're not putting all our funding in the future and sacrificing the present.

asr-007014
04:57:55.880 --> 04:57:56.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So I don't know.

asr-007015
04:57:56.960 --> 04:57:59.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: If I ask now, what is the balancing act?

asr-007016
04:57:59.360 --> 04:58:00.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Can I get an answer?

asr-007017
04:58:00.280 --> 04:58:03.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Like, what are we, do we know?

asr-007018
04:58:03.960 --> 04:58:10.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What kind of funding are we doing that is an investment in the future versus investing today?

asr-007019
04:58:10.660 --> 04:58:14.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And my favorite agency as the chairman also is health, right?

asr-007020
04:58:14.840 --> 04:58:17.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So if we say immunization, then that's for the future.

asr-007021
04:58:17.720 --> 04:58:18.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Clear tayo?

asr-007022
04:58:18.220 --> 04:58:18.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Diba?

asr-007023
04:58:19.140 --> 04:58:26.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's not something that will save a life of a child with malaria right now, and not malaria, measles right now.

asr-007024
04:58:26.660 --> 04:58:28.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's too late to give them the measles vaccination.

asr-007025
04:58:29.440 --> 04:58:31.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So that's the future of this child's life.

asr-007026
04:58:31.780 --> 04:58:37.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We should know how much of our funding goes into future planning and how much is stopgap,

asr-007027
04:58:37.720 --> 04:58:39.920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: which on the one hand, you might consider ayuda.

asr-007028
04:58:40.100 --> 04:58:41.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's not necessarily ayuda.

asr-007029
04:58:41.220 --> 04:58:48.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I mean, if you say you're purchasing fast-growing crops for next year's season,

asr-007030
04:58:48.220 --> 04:58:49.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that's not ayuda.

asr-007031
04:58:49.680 --> 04:58:52.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's feeding people today and tomorrow.

asr-007032
04:58:53.080 --> 04:59:01.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But future planning requires that you're saving part of those seedlings for the next 10 years, 20 years,

asr-007033
04:59:01.180 --> 04:59:03.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: you're banking these seeds, and so on and so forth.

asr-007034
04:59:03.620 --> 04:59:06.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Do we even have that kind of data, Mr. President, Mr. Chairman?

asr-007037
04:59:44.560 --> 04:59:46.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Your Honor, Mr. President,

asr-007049
04:59:46.120 --> 04:59:54.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: They are now preparing the intergenerational report that will span 25 years.

asr-007050
04:59:56.140 --> 04:59:59.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So they are currently consolidating.

asr-007051
05:00:00.000 --> 05:00:07.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And it will be due for release first quarter, Your Honor, Mr. President.

asr-007052
05:00:07.720 --> 05:00:14.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's great, Mr. President, because I think most agencies would have their...

asr-007053
05:00:24.000 --> 05:00:27.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Anyway, we're all guided by the Philippine Development Plan, di ba?

asr-007054
05:00:27.280 --> 05:00:31.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero, from what I recall, it's like agency-based.

asr-007055
05:00:32.300 --> 05:00:39.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I like this, that it is focused on the human beings, that what will their life look like 25 years.

asr-007056
05:00:40.060 --> 05:00:45.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But take note, that's just one generation. May mga bansa nga, seven generations nga.

asr-007057
05:00:45.580 --> 05:00:49.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I think yung 25 na yan, because I've been a senator for 20 years.

asr-007058
05:00:49.880 --> 05:00:56.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, technically, my legislation is contributed to whatever outcomes we see.

asr-007059
05:00:57.280 --> 05:01:01.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And don't see, because that's almost the 25 years that you're talking about.

asr-007060
05:01:01.960 --> 05:01:05.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, anyway, I leave that all with you. Thank you.

asr-007061
05:01:06.500 --> 05:01:09.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'll go now to a bit of the economic forecast, no?

asr-007062
05:01:10.040 --> 05:01:11.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We understand that...

asr-007063
05:01:11.940 --> 05:01:23.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think I'll use ADB's figures that says, by 2027, we expect there to be a better...

asr-007064
05:01:23.340 --> 05:01:26.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I don't know what part of 2027 this is, maybe you can fill me in.

asr-007065
05:01:26.480 --> 05:01:27.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: At what part?

asr-007066
05:01:27.200 --> 05:01:27.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: At what part?

asr-007067
05:01:27.280 --> 05:01:38.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: At what part of 2027 do we see our growth picking up a bit from, I think, the last number you gave, Senator Riza, was 3%, mid, second quarter, third quarter, fourth quarter?

asr-007068
05:01:38.280 --> 05:01:41.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then the follow-up question, para isang sagutan na lang, why?

asr-007069
05:01:41.620 --> 05:01:57.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What will happen, whatever that quarter is, what will happen in that amount of time that gives us the comfort in knowing that there will be economic growth by then?

asr-007070
05:01:57.200 --> 05:01:57.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What will happen, whatever that quarter is, what will happen in that amount of time that gives us the comfort in knowing that there will be economic growth by then?

asr-007071
05:02:00.200 --> 05:02:20.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mr. President, according to Secretary De Leon, the improvement can be felt already by first quarter, because it will be the spillover expected in the fourth quarter momentum will be carried over, plus the fact that they will...

asr-007072
05:02:20.020 --> 05:02:22.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sorry, please educate me, the spillover of what?

asr-007073
05:02:22.440 --> 05:02:26.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Of the implementation of the infrastructure.

asr-007074
05:02:27.200 --> 05:02:55.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Of the implementation of the infrastructure projects, kasi po, second half na of this year, that were procured and awarded, so they expect that third and fourth quarter will slowly gain momentum, it will be carried during the first quarter, and at the same, plus that they will implement early procurement for 2027, so they expect...

asr-007075
05:02:55.200 --> 05:02:56.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: They expect...

asr-007076
05:02:57.200 --> 05:03:03.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That the award will likely, they will be able to award also during the first quarter, so...

asr-007077
05:03:03.480 --> 05:03:09.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, I'll fill in the gap, because this is a discussion that was had, I think, in the interpellation of other senators, no?

asr-007078
05:03:09.880 --> 05:03:25.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, you're saying that because spending in funding, spending in DPWH is down, that's because of the time it took to whatever, whatever that process is.

asr-007079
05:03:25.860 --> 05:03:27.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ngayon pa lang may implement.

asr-007080
05:03:27.040 --> 05:03:27.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ngayon pa lang may implement.

asr-007081
05:03:27.200 --> 05:03:34.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: In the fourth quarter, so makikita yung effect na yun, because everybody's questioning why the spending was so low, so dun makikita yun.

asr-007082
05:03:34.120 --> 05:03:37.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, in other words, what is the effect on our normal kababayan?

asr-007083
05:03:37.500 --> 05:03:50.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung mga nasa construction work, expect nyo na you will have jobs in the first quarter of 2027, that's what we're saying, because it's non-existence in the province, so that's what we're saying, there will be jobs.

asr-007084
05:03:51.560 --> 05:03:51.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes?

asr-007085
05:03:52.200 --> 05:03:57.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: There should be, according to our secretary of DVM, by first quarter.

asr-007086
05:03:57.200 --> 05:04:03.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: As chairman of the committee, Mr. Chairman, paano papatawag tayo ng hearing by the end of the first quarter to get updates?

asr-007087
05:04:03.400 --> 05:04:06.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I mean, we don't have to bother anyone if it's looking good, no?

asr-007088
05:04:06.760 --> 05:04:10.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But if not, kasi this is what we're telling people, eh.

asr-007089
05:04:10.860 --> 05:04:11.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, sir.

asr-007090
05:04:11.240 --> 05:04:18.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: They agree that we should be calling DPWH for updates regarding the...

asr-007091
05:04:18.480 --> 05:04:22.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes, so on paper, on paper, this is what the economic team is saying.

asr-007092
05:04:22.740 --> 05:04:23.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes.

asr-007093
05:04:23.100 --> 05:04:26.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, of course, it's DPWH we expect to implement that.

asr-007094
05:04:27.200 --> 05:04:37.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, can we ask the economic team to mention, to share some input about manufacturing?

asr-007095
05:04:37.940 --> 05:04:38.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We're not up, right?

asr-007096
05:04:38.760 --> 05:04:39.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We're also down.

asr-007097
05:04:39.280 --> 05:04:39.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We're also down.

asr-007098
05:04:48.740 --> 05:04:53.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The industry as a whole is, according to Secretary Balisakan, is zero.

asr-007099
05:04:54.340 --> 05:04:54.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Zero?

asr-007100
05:04:54.900 --> 05:04:55.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As in flat.

asr-007101
05:04:55.660 --> 05:04:57.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ah, so not negative.

asr-007102
05:04:57.200 --> 05:04:58.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, wait, what's a zero?

asr-007103
05:04:58.820 --> 05:05:00.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, zero compared to what?

asr-007104
05:05:00.800 --> 05:05:01.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: No growth.

asr-007105
05:05:02.920 --> 05:05:08.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, no growth compared to a month ago, compared to year on year?

asr-007106
05:05:08.980 --> 05:05:10.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Same period last year.

asr-007107
05:05:10.620 --> 05:05:10.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yun.

asr-007108
05:05:11.340 --> 05:05:12.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Same period last year.

asr-007109
05:05:12.220 --> 05:05:12.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: No growth.

asr-007110
05:05:13.300 --> 05:05:13.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: No growth.

asr-007111
05:05:15.660 --> 05:05:16.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-007112
05:05:17.480 --> 05:05:22.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What does that mean as far as the average Filipino is concerned when there's no growth?

asr-007113
05:05:22.300 --> 05:05:22.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I don't know.

asr-007114
05:05:22.820 --> 05:05:23.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's why I'm asking.

asr-007115
05:05:23.600 --> 05:05:24.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What does that mean?

asr-007116
05:05:25.660 --> 05:05:26.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: No.

asr-007117
05:05:26.380 --> 05:05:26.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: No.

asr-007118
05:05:27.200 --> 05:05:28.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: You know, new jobs created.

asr-007119
05:05:29.000 --> 05:05:29.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: No new jobs.

asr-007120
05:05:29.980 --> 05:05:30.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes.

asr-007121
05:05:30.400 --> 05:05:33.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero the existing jobs supposedly are still there.

asr-007122
05:05:34.300 --> 05:05:35.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi it's not down.

asr-007123
05:05:35.600 --> 05:05:37.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's just not up.

asr-007124
05:05:41.420 --> 05:05:43.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Existing jobs are still there.

asr-007125
05:05:43.860 --> 05:05:45.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But there's no expansion.

asr-007126
05:05:46.600 --> 05:05:47.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kapit pa rin.

asr-007127
05:05:48.360 --> 05:05:51.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, Senator Camila has a question.

asr-007128
05:05:51.160 --> 05:05:51.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Good question.

asr-007129
05:05:52.160 --> 05:05:53.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, year on year.

asr-007130
05:05:53.720 --> 05:05:55.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, zero from 2025.

asr-007131
05:05:56.220 --> 05:05:57.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We're in the last quarter.

asr-007132
05:05:57.020 --> 05:06:03.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, what was it from 2025, fourth quarter, compared to 2024?

asr-007133
05:06:04.420 --> 05:06:05.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yun, may growth pa yun?

asr-007134
05:06:06.520 --> 05:06:09.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm trying to remember kasi when did our luck turn so bad?

asr-007135
05:06:10.640 --> 05:06:18.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: According to them, according to the economic managers, yes, there's growth during those periods.

asr-007136
05:06:18.840 --> 05:06:19.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What was the growth rate?

asr-007137
05:06:20.260 --> 05:06:20.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Do we know?

asr-007138
05:06:21.340 --> 05:06:21.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Do we recall?

asr-007139
05:06:21.940 --> 05:06:22.920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Can we quickly check lang?

asr-007140
05:06:23.980 --> 05:06:24.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Like one.

asr-007145
05:06:52.380 --> 05:06:55.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And while they're looking for more details to provide,

asr-007152
05:06:56.940 --> 05:06:58.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Can we just compare ourselves with our neighbors?

asr-007153
05:06:58.960 --> 05:07:03.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: In the third quarter of this year, Vietnam's economy expanded by 9.95%,

asr-007154
05:07:03.220 --> 05:07:04.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: almost 10% year on year,

asr-007155
05:07:05.340 --> 05:07:08.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: nearly twice the rate recorded by Indonesia, Singapore, and Malaysia,

asr-007156
05:07:08.440 --> 05:07:10.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: which all grew by around 5%.

asr-007157
05:07:10.680 --> 05:07:13.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So we lag last.

asr-007158
05:07:14.360 --> 05:07:18.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So sad for us.

asr-007159
05:07:20.900 --> 05:07:26.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The difference is Vietnam concentrated really in developing

asr-007160
05:07:26.480 --> 05:07:30.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: their industries, especially the export industry.

asr-007161
05:07:31.360 --> 05:07:33.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But we revised CREATE again.

asr-007162
05:07:33.900 --> 05:07:35.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I was the author of CREATE,

asr-007163
05:07:36.120 --> 05:07:41.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: which was a pandemic law that I worked on.

asr-007164
05:07:42.480 --> 05:07:46.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then under this administration, CREATE agad nirevise.

asr-007165
05:07:46.960 --> 05:07:48.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So did it bring results?

asr-007166
05:07:50.320 --> 05:07:55.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: According to the RDIF Secretary, that export is up last.

asr-007167
05:07:56.480 --> 05:08:00.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But this year, it's about 16%.

asr-007168
